/24/335324/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I3a4a8dbe10df48898d802dd84175690756d9a90a" commit="c57ca47b938430526dc26045b5b2dd3ffd84900c" commit_message="Revert &quot;FROMLIST: ASoC: nau8825: extend FLL functions&quot;  This reverts commit d082ed7dcfd364d49056988f52d6f62d1f70bef5. The reverted commit is replaced by (&quot;ASoC: nau8825: support different clock source for FLL function&quot;) (&quot;ASoC: nau8825: improve FLL function for better performance&quot;)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: I3a4a8dbe10df48898d802dd84175690756d9a90a Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335668 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335668" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/68/335668/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I5041a5d56ba687ba9524ac7482233dabb04b1e10" commit="7f793358bac944ccef79bab9d78f9cd3d2a9117a" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: support different clock source for FLL function  Extend FLL clock source selection. The source can be from MCLK, BCLK or FS.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit ac61ae979d92cb99c18c938f5854179ed54d111a) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: I5041a5d56ba687ba9524ac7482233dabb04b1e10 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335669 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335669" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/69/335669/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I04a9268a17ba1a0b4fa1d2b04d5e22fdc66aaaa0" commit="3602cdf2efa99126fbea20f50c071262d4c2f5a5" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: improve FLL function for better performance  In FLL calculation, increase VCO/DCO frequency for better performance. Besides, have different register configuration according to fraction or not when apply FLL parameters.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5d4e244cd2c7a4ab9f8947da4ef40eccdfd15e74) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: I04a9268a17ba1a0b4fa1d2b04d5e22fdc66aaaa0 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335910 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335910" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/335910/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I73417c847a8d87738c0ddf02aa371bcd1fb85b74" commit="ec208ed6087845ecfd210ddc5169bc4d4ac8f9d6" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: reduce standby power consumption  Decrease internal clock frequency for power saving when standby. But clock divider needs restore when MCLK as system clock in playback.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5a78e7c37d5d27702fdc019d610361c95491f989) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: I73417c847a8d87738c0ddf02aa371bcd1fb85b74 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335911 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335911" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/11/335911/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="If51ce47aafdf2b21f1b95d34ec28c8570fca0595" commit="de7602b498863a53764f45f83cdfaf28e0998ad8" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: change output power for interrupt  The interrupt clock is gated by x1[10:8], one of them needs to be enabled all the time for interrupts to happen. We change codec to enable ADC because it's helpful to reduce playback pop noise. Don't use force enable pin to enable ADC instead of ADC widget event. That won't interfere DAPM operation and let bias work normally.  Signed-off-by: John Hsu &lt;KCHSU0@nuvoton.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit fcd576e2b9872b3588f72352d9f50adc03876118) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: If51ce47aafdf2b21f1b95d34ec28c8570fca0595 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335912 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335912" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/12/335912/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I79e449c0988647e244f225fc7ea5c8b97ed37f58" commit="474c91783924d87008f56d3eb8db46c751f70f0d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: nau8825: Fix jack detection across suspend  Jack plug status is rechecked at resume to handle plug/unplug in S3 when the chip has no power.  Suspend/resume callbacks are moved from the i2c dev_pm_ops to snd_soc_codec_driver. soc_resume_deferred is a delayed work which may trigger nau8825_set_bias_level. The bias change races against dev_pm_ops, causing jack detection issues. soc_resume_deferred ensures bias change and snd_soc_codec_driver suspend/resume are sequenced correctly.  Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit e6cee90075c0ff261ff7eef8ad892429f028e194) Signed-off-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50336 TEST=Combinations of headset plug/unplug, s3/s0ix suspend/resume, with/without doing playback on Chell.  Change-Id: I79e449c0988647e244f225fc7ea5c8b97ed37f58 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/335325 Commit-Ready: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Ben Zhang &lt;benzh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="335325" owner_email="benzh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/25/335325/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Id069092f85e841e80693c299aa9fecf02fcba4d5" commit="aaadea3ea4b15b087049b50591de737b355b5ab3" commit_message="FROMLIST: clk: qcom: ipq4019: switch remaining defines to enums  When this was added not all the remaining defines were switched over to use enums, so let's complete that process here  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49255 TEST=Changing BAUD rate on serial port to HS does not crash  Change-Id: Id069092f85e841e80693c299aa9fecf02fcba4d5 Reported-by: Stephen Boyd &lt;sboyd@codeaurora.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8655081/) Signed-off-by: Matthew McClintock &lt;mmcclint@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334858 Commit-Ready: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334858" owner_email="mmcclint@qca.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/58/334858/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I33cdead8d221c88b5e63a058a46008635209a8d0" commit="8f29361575d479a43f05d4839300499f9a4190b1" commit_message="FROMLIST: clk: qcom: ipq4019: add some fixed clocks for ddrppl and fepll  Drivers for these don't exist yet so we will add them as fixed clocks so we don't BUG() if we change clocks that reference these clocks.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49255 TEST=Changing BAUD rate on serial port to HS does not crash  Change-Id: I33cdead8d221c88b5e63a058a46008635209a8d0 (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8655071/) Signed-off-by: Matthew McClintock &lt;mmcclint@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334859 Commit-Ready: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: D